A:  Parking

 When you choose plan 1 ,the fee will be A × N yen,and when you choose plan 2, the fee will
be B yen.
  So,it is good to print the smaller of A × N and B.

#include <cstdio >
int N,A,B;
int main ()
{
         scanf ("%d%d%d",&N,&A,&B);
        if(N*A<=B)printf ("%d\n",N*A);
         else printf ("%d\n",B);
}



B:  Harshad Number

  For example,f(N) can be calculated as such.
  1: Set t = N,c = 0.
  2: Add to c ,the remainder of t divided by 10.
  3: Substitute the quotient of t divided by 10 ,for t.
  4: If t > 0,go 2. If t = 0,quit. Then c = f(N).
  After that, it is good to check is N can be divided by f(N) or not.

#include <cstdio >
int N;
int main ()
{
         scanf ("%d",&N);
         int t=N,c=0;
        while(t>0)c+=t%10,t/=10;
        if(N%c==0) puts ("Yes ");
         else puts ("No");
}





